{
  "source_id": "county-096",
  "text": "Board of Elections | Wayne County, NC\nSkip to Main Content\nGovernment\nDepartments\nCommunity\nServices\neGov\nSearch\nHome\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\n2026 Election Information:\nNovember 3, 2026 General Election\nEarly Voting Schedule\nDaily List of Early Voters\n/\nEarly Voting Statistics\nSample Ballots (combined)\n/\nSample Ballot Voter Search Tool\nCandidate & Referendum List\nJudicial Voter Guide\nElection Notice\n/\nUOCAVA Election Notice\n/\nBuffer Zone Notice\nElection Calendar\nResolution to Add Absentee Meetings\nNotice of Election Day Precinct #2530 Change\n/\nPrecinct #2530 Precinct Change Flyer\nEach county in North Carolina has a Board of Elections. It is a five-person bipartisan board appointed every two years by the State Board of Elections. County Board members take an oath and begin their two-year terms on the Tuesday following the third Monday in July in odd-numbered years.\nResponsibilities of the Board of Elections\nThe Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all elections held in Wayne County. The Board administers, locally, State election laws. Principal functions include establishing election precincts and voting sites; appointing and training precinct officials; preparing and distributing ballots and voting equipment; canvassing and certifying the ballots cast in elections; and investigating any voting irregularities. It maintains voter registration, voting records, and provides public information on voters and elections.\nUpcoming:\nOct. 20th Notice - Absentee\n/\nAgenda\nOct. 27th Notice - Absentee\n/\nAgenda\nNov. 2nd Notice - Absentee\nNov. 3rd Notice - Election Day/Absentee\nNov. 5th Notice - Sample Audit Count\nNov. 10th Notice - Absentee/Provisional\nNov. 12th Notice - Absentee/Canvass Prep\nNov. 13th Notice - County Canvass\nQuick Links:\nVoter Search Link\nVoter Reg/Update Form\nVoter Reg/Update Form (Spanish)\nDMV Voter Reg Portal\nAbsentee Ballot Portal\n2026 Absentee Ballot Request Form\nPrecinct Official Application\nContact Information:\n309 East Chestnut St.\nGoldsboro, NC 27530\nPhone: (919) 731-1411\nFax: (919) 731-1409\nEmail: elections@waynegov.com\nVoter Information\nCheck My Registration\nRegister to Vote\nVoter Photo ID\nStudent & Public Employee IDs Approved for Voting\nAbsentee Voting\nUOCAVA Voter Info\nWhere's My Polling Place?\nAll Polling Locations\nEarly Voting Sites\nVoter Registration Stats\nBack to Main\nCandidate Information\nCampaign Finance\nPrecinct Officials\nOnline Application\nStudent Election Assistant Application\nQualifications\nStatutes\n2025-2027 Appointees\nBack to Main\nResources\nElected Officials\nElection Results\nData & Public Records Requests\nData & Public Records Request Form\nMaps\nBack to Main\nForms and Documents\nBoard Information\nAgendas & Minutes\nPay Taxes\nCareers\nAdopt a Pet\nLibrary\nSheriff's Office\nContact Us\nWayne County Courthouse\n224 E Walnut Street\nGoldsboro, NC 27530\nQuick Links\nPay Taxes Online\nJob Opportunities\nCommissioners Meetings - Live Stream\nGovDeals - County surplus for sale\nThe Maxwell Center - Official Website\nMunicipal Code / County Ordinances\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHelpful Links\nHome\nCopyright Notices\nAccessibility\nSite Map\nBoard Portal\nEmployee Login\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
